  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Inside Hei tribe’s hall he stares at the first supreme elder with an indomitable gaze and argues for fighting. After hearing the tribe’s decision he shakes, takes a deep breath, and feels intense sorrow rather than rage, then laughs and leads the Gu Immortals out to face the enemies.",
      "chapters": [
        1108
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "fac_hei_tribe",
        "sys_gu_immortal"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Dark light shines from his eyes when he fights.",
      "chapters": [
        1109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "eyes-in-battle",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "With him as leader, seven rank six Gu Immortals stand behind him before the invaders. Liu Zhuan Shen names him an old rival fought more than a hundred times. He opens with immortal killer move life draining darkness, a costly trump card rarely used at the start of battle. He can expend lifespan to raise killer move power, and his battle strength exceeds Pi Shui Han’s without reaching rank eight. He drives Guan Chou’s lion form away like a rag doll, chases across the field, and remains the last Hei tribe fighter until he is out of immortal essence and dies. Afterward Chu Du is judged far stronger than he was.",
      "chapters": [
        1109
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "final-defense-and-death",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "char_liu_zhuan_shen",
        "char_pi_shui_han",
        "char_guan_chou",
        "char_chu_du"
      ]
    }
